{"id": "EUVD-2026-106993", "enisaUuid": "7aa70eb8-7c37-35ac-866f-f477f78e0f3c", "description": "FreeRDP 3.32.0 contains a use-after-free vulnerability in the drdynvc channel that frees a pool-owned stream with the owned-stream deallocator when totalLength is smaller than the chunk size. A malicious RDP server can send a single well-formed Virtual Channel PDU to trigger the free and crash the client during teardown.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:36:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T18:23:03", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-5xjc-c64q-m8r6", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-3.32.0-use-after-free-via-drdynvc-virtual-channel-pdu"], "aliases": ["GHSA-72vv-4hwf-qhx6", "CVE-2026-114042"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b1fbafce-074b-3ef5-8976-506a9ad268cd", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.32.0 <3.32.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "18ac1460-7b87-3456-93d8-88bb00db3c1f", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}